{"name":"Burning Gold","hex":"#ccaa77","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"burning","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of burn"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["So hot as to seem to burn (something).","Feeling very hot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burning"},{"term":"gold","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy yellow elemental metal of great value, with atomic number 79.","A coin or coinage made of this material, or supposedly so."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["☉ (alchemy)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gold"}],"entries":[{"title":"Burning Gold (1927 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Burning Gold is a 1927 American silent drama film directed by John W. Noble and starring Herbert Rawlinson, Shirley Palmer and Sheldon Lewis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Burning_Gold_%281927_film%29.jpg/330px-Burning_Gold_%281927_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burning_Gold_(1927_film)"},{"title":"Burning Gold (1936 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Burning Gold is a 1936 American drama film directed by Sam Newfield and starring William Boyd, Judith Allen and Lloyd Ingraham. It is a modern-day western about a World War I veteran who becomes a wildcat prospector for oil and enjoys a major strike."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/54/Burning_Gold_1936_poster.jpg/330px-Burning_Gold_1936_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burning_Gold_(1936_film)"},{"title":"Burning Gold (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Burning Gold\" is a song by American singer-songwriter Christina Perri for her second studio album, Head or Heart (2014). The song was written by Perri and Kid Harpoon and produced by John Hill and Butch Walker. It was first released through the iTunes Store as a promotional single for Head or Heart on March 11, 2014, and was subsequently released as the second single from the album on June 9. The song was used on seventh episode of second season of the American TV series, The Fosters."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/13/BurningGold-ChristinaPerri.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burning_Gold_(song)"},{"title":"Combustion","blocks":[{"text":"Combustion, or burning, is a high-temperature exothermic redox chemical reaction between a fuel and an oxidant, usually atmospheric oxygen, that produces oxidized, often gaseous products, in a mixture termed as smoke. Combustion does not always result in fire, because a flame is only visible when substances undergoing combustion vaporize, but when it does, a flame is a characteristic indicator of the reaction. While activation energy must be supplied to initiate combustion, the heat from a flame may provide enough energy to make the reaction self-sustaining. The study of combustion is known as combustion science."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Fire%2C_Fireplace%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg/330px-Fire%2C_Fireplace%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Combustion"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Regenerative_thermal_oxidizer.jpg/500px-Regenerative_thermal_oxidizer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Regenerative_thermal_oxidizer.jpg/1280px-Regenerative_thermal_oxidizer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Regenerative_thermal_oxidizer.jpg/500px-Regenerative_thermal_oxidizer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Air pollution abatement equipment provides combustion control for industrial processes.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARegenerative_thermal_oxidizer.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Microgravity_Burning.jpg/500px-Microgravity_Burning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Microgravity_Burning.jpg/1280px-Microgravity_Burning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Microgravity_Burning.jpg/500px-Microgravity_Burning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Colourized gray-scale composite image of the individual frames from a video of a backlit fuel droplet burning in microgravity","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMicrogravity_Burning.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Zoom_lunette_ardente.jpg/500px-Zoom_lunette_ardente.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Zoom_lunette_ardente.jpg/500px-Zoom_lunette_ardente.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Antoine Lavoisier conducting an experiment related to combustion generated by amplified sunlight","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZoom_lunette_ardente.jpg"}],"sounds":{"burning":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/41/En-us-burning.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/41/En-us-burning.ogg/En-us-burning.ogg.mp3"}],"gold":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.w